course: dictionary
lesson: 11801
title: Besieged: surrounded and overwhelmed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Besieged means surrounded. In history, an army besieges a castle or town to capture it, so the people inside cannot leave or get food. «The king's army besieged the castle for three months.» The clues are army, castle and months, so besieged means the castle was surrounded for a long time.
explain: Besieged also describes a crowd. «The singer was besieged by fans outside the hotel.» Nobody attacked the singer with an army. The fans crowded round because they wanted something, such as an autograph or a photo. Use the swap check: put your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Besieged can also mean bothered by many requests, questions or problems. «The teacher was besieged with questions after the test.» Those questions were like a crowd pressing in, so the teacher had far too many to answer. Ask yourself what is pressing in on the person or place.
fact: «Besieged» is the past form of the verb «besiege», so it describes something that has already been surrounded.
fact: «Besieged» means surrounded by an army that is trying to capture a town or castle.
fact: «Besieged» can also mean crowded by many people who want something, such as fans or shoppers.
fact: «Besieged» can mean bothered by a great many requests, questions or problems.
fact: When you meet besieged, look for clues such as army, crowd, fans or questions, to see which meaning fits.
exercise: «The town was besieged by the enemy army for months.» What does besieged mean? | Asked to leave quickly | *Surrounded by an army trying to capture it | Celebrated with a big party | Painted in bright colours
exercise: Find and copy the one word from «The shop was besieged by shoppers on sale day» that means surrounded by a crowd who want something. | *besieged | sale | shop | day
exercise: «The teacher was besieged with questions after the test.» What does besieged suggest? | Fell asleep in class | Was asked to go home early | Was given a prize for good work | *Had far too many questions to answer
test: «The famous singer was besieged by fans at the airport.» What does besieged mean here? | Cleaned and dried | Sleeping peacefully | Safely hidden from view | *Crowded round by many people who want something
test: Mum says, «I'm besieged with emails today.» What does she mean? | *She has a great many emails to deal with | She is going on holiday | She has no emails at all | She is writing a letter to the king
exam: «After the flood, the rescue team was besieged by requests for help.» What does besieged mean? | Was moved to a sunny island | *Had far too many requests to deal with | Was asked to sing a song | Had no work to do
